os32-font — T7b shared crate (not connected to shell/shlib yet)

src/limits.rs is the single definition of the T7b-a1 corpus limits for
IPAex 004.01 and Inconsolata Regular 3.000. These are bounds for later
readers, not a promise of arbitrary TrueType support. No allocations or
resident tables are introduced in a1.

vendor/ttf-parser-0.21.1 contains upstream src/, Cargo.toml, Cargo.toml.orig,
README.md and both license originals, byte-for-byte from the crates.io
archive. OS32 selects MIT (LICENSE-MIT). Examples, tests and dev tooling
are omitted. UPSTREAM.json records the archive URL/hash and each retained
file hash. No source patch. Both dependencies use default-features=false.

API boundary (T7b-a1 investigation): Face::parse/from_raw_tables require
borrowed slices and have no read_at callback. Later readers must handle
SFNT directory/scalars, cmap 4/12, loca/hmtx and component collection/gid
rewriting. Public loca::Table::parse + glyf::Table::parse/outline can read
a bounded temporary glyf/loca for one glyph and its components; private
simple-outline/composite iterators are not used. Do not connect the
prototype's whole-file Face::parse to the product.

Final linked 386 instruction validation remains the T7b-a5 gate (D36).
The dependency version/features remain unchanged.

T7b-a3/a4: reader::Face owns its Source and fixed LRU, and provides streaming
cmap/loca/advance access. outline::GlyphScratch::outline(face, gid) gathers
one glyph and each component occurrence through that LRU, validates spans,
expanded points/contours, runs, components and depth, rewrites local gids,
and invokes only public loca/glyf tables. XY components (including matrices)
are supported; point attachment/scaled component offsets return Unsupported.
An Err publishes zero committed counts, including after a previous success.
Outline borrows bounded points, contour edge ranges and line/quadratic edges
in font units, with the same command sequence/bbox as whole-file Face.
MAX_POINTS counts stored glyf points; MAX_OUTLINE_POINTS also accommodates
implicit midpoints and closing commands. MAX_EDGES bounds curve edges here;
a5 must enforce it again after flattening. Scratch is caller-owned and can be
shared serially between faces; use the a2 x87 guard on OS32. No raster, bitmap
cache, source lease, shell/shlib connection or new module is added by a4.

check-font-outline-host compares the complete a1 JIS/Latin corpora against
whole-file ttf-parser Face (JF Shinonome16, Inconsolata, both IPAex originals),
and expects the a1 unsupported/exceeded list to remain empty. Synthetic SFNTs
exercise each independent bound, repeated components, cycle/run corruption
and every cold-read failure, including successful retry and zero publication.
